  "version": "2026-10-11b",
  "about": "Airport positions for the cargo journey map. These point at the airport, not at the city centre, and they are map positions - not surveyed reference points and never an aircraft position. Names are the forms carriers actually send us (a code, or free text such as NARITA or PU DONG); aliases hold those forms exactly so a whole city is never matched to an airport.",
  "source": "Well-established public airport locations, written here by hand. No external dataset was downloaded.",
  "accuracy": "Two decimal places is about one kilometre, which is the scale this map draws at.",
  "review": "Three entries moved or are ambiguous in real life and are worth a second look: TAO (Qingdao moved to Jiaodong in 2021), UBN (Ulaanbaatar moved to the new airport in 2021), and PEK (free text 'BEIJING' is read as Capital, not Daxing).",
